Thank you for taking time to look at my problem. I had previously tried just running the model on the covariates only but felt that it could be improved by adding spatial random effects.

If I may ask, wouldn't the issue of overfitting persist regardless of the number of observations/regions for this type of modelling (BYM2)? For example, if I had 1000 observations, that would imply at least 2000 parameters in the model. I followed the same analysis steps the authors from this paper <https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-022-00905-1> took and found they had similar overfitting issues (however only to 3 decimal places rather than my 5), although they had more than 6000 observations.

Is the BYM specification not ideal in general for this type of data?

Kind regards,
John

